---
import Marketing from '../layouts/Marketing.astro';
---

<Marketing
  title="Grossline — what it does"
  description="Grossline reads your Shopify store and your ad accounts together, works out what you actually kept, and sends one short monthly report with the few things worth changing."
  path="/what-it-does"
>
  <div class="pagehead">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">What it does</div>
      <h1>One place where your sales and your ad spend <em>finally agree</em>.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Grossline reads your Shopify store and your Google and Meta ad accounts together, works out
        what you actually kept after every cost, and hands you a short monthly report with the two or
        three things worth changing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section style="padding-top:56px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">How it works</div>
      <h2>Connect once. Then a report just arrives.</h2>
      <div class="cols">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="idx">01</div>
          <h3>You connect your accounts</h3>
          <p>
            Your Shopify store and your Google and Meta ad accounts. We ask for read-only access,
            which means we can look but never change anything in your store or your campaigns.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="idx">02</div>
          <h3>We put the numbers together</h3>
          <p>
            Your orders, your ad spend and your costs land untouched, then we work out the numbers
            that actually matter: what you kept, whether your ads paid for themselves, and what a new
            customer costs — all in your store's own timezone.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="idx">03</div>
          <h3>You get a report and a call</h3>
          <p>
            A short monthly report with the headline, where your money went, where the platforms
            disagree with your store, what changed, and the few things worth doing — checked against
            Shopify and your ad platforms before you ever see it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">The numbers, done properly</div>
      <h2>Counted, not guessed.</h2>
      <div class="cols two">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>We count what happened, not what a pixel thinks happened</h3>
          <p>
            No tracking pixels, no attribution guesswork. Just what was sold and what it cost to sell
            it, across every channel at once — the real total, not one platform's version of it.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Honest by construction</h3>
          <p>
            Every figure is exact to the cent, and carries its currency. When a cost is missing we
            show the number as incomplete, never as zero. Each report says when it was last pulled and
            last checked.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Findings, not dashboards</div>
      <h2>A few things to do — not a wall of charts.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Each month you get a short, ranked list of findings. They come in two kinds, and the report
        never blurs them.
      </p>
      <div class="cols two">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Where money is leaking</h3>
          <p>
            Ads that aren't paying for themselves, new customers who cost more than their first order
            brings back, discounts creeping up, spend running ahead of plan. Real savings, ranked by
            the money at stake.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Where there's room to grow</h3>
          <p>
            When your ads are working well, where the spare budget could go — put as a small, bounded
            test with a check the following month, because what works at today's spend won't
            automatically hold at triple the budget.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="demo-note">
        What we can find depends on the data your store connects; the report says plainly what it
        could and could not measure that month.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding-top:0;padding-bottom:96px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <a class="btn" href="/free-report">Get your first report free</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Marketing>
